      "locked": false,
      "text": "- roadmap.sh/backend — community-curated backend developer roadmap\n- FastAPI official docs (fastapi.tiangolo.com) — async Python API framework, strong on typing/validation\n- Django official docs (docs.djangoproject.com) — batteries-included framework, ORM/migrations reference\n- Flask official docs (flask.palletsprojects.com) — minimal WSGI framework, good for understanding fundamentals\n- \"Designing Data-Intensive Applications\" by Martin Kleppmann — the canonical book on databases, caching, and distributed systems tradeoffs\n- \"System Design Interview\" by Alex Xu (Vol. 1 & 2) — walks through the rate limiter / URL shortener / notification-service archetypes\n- donnemartin/system-design-primer (GitHub) — widely-used open-source system design interview reference\n- PostgreSQL official docs, transaction isolation chapter (postgresql.org/docs) — authoritative reference on isolation levels and concurrency",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- roadmap.sh/backend — community-curated backend developer roadmap\n- FastAPI official docs (fastapi.tiangolo.com) — async Python API framework, strong on typing/validation\n- Django official docs (docs.djangoproject.com) — batteries-included framework, ORM/migrations reference\n- Flask official docs (flask.palletsprojects.com) — minimal WSGI framework, good for understanding fundamentals\n- \"Designing Data-Intensive Applications\" by Martin Kleppmann — the canonical book on databases, caching, and distributed systems tradeoffs\n- \"System Design Interview\" by Alex Xu (Vol. 1 & 2) — walks through the rate limiter / URL shortener / notification-service archetypes\n- donnemartin/system-design-primer (GitHub) — widely-used open-source system design interview reference\n- PostgreSQL official docs, transaction isolation chapter (postgresql.org/docs) — authoritative reference on isolation levels and concurrency",
